{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Camera Placement.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Camera Placement.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"programmatic blender camera placement programmatic blender camera placement","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Camera Placement.md","fileName":"Programmatic Blender Camera Placement.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Programmatic Blender Camera Placement","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 09:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Camera Placement.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Camera Placement.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"programmatic blender camera placement programmatic blender camera placement","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Camera Placement.md","fileName":"Programmatic Blender Camera Placement.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Programmatic Blender Camera Placement","heading":"Programmatic Blender Camera Placement","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Automated camera placement must position and aim a camera so the generated scene fits within its field of view. The scene's aggregate bounding box supplies a center and size, while the render resolution determines the image aspect ratio.\n\nFor a camera aligned with an axis, trigonometry relates half the scene width or height to half the corresponding field-of-view angle. The larger required distance frames both dimensions, and a small buffer avoids touching the image edges. The camera can then be aimed from its computed location toward the bounding-box center.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Camera Placement.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Camera Placement.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"programmatic blender camera placement programmatic blender camera placement","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Programmatic Blender Camera Placement.md","fileName":"Programmatic Blender Camera Placement.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Programmatic Blender Camera Placement","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[blenderpythonapi.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Automated Blender Texturing and Rendering","blenderpythonapi.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}